---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms — Wyllex"
  description="Terms for the Wyllex website and early access waitlist."
>
  <section class="legal-main" data-theme="light">
    <article class="legal-content">
      <div class="eyebrow">A FEW THINGS TO KNOW.</div>
      <h1>The terms.</h1>
      <p class="legal-date">Last updated {site.legal.updated}</p>
      <p class="legal-intro">
        These terms cover your use of the Wyllex website and early access waitlist, operated by{' '}
        {site.legal.operator}. By using the site or joining the list, you agree to these terms.
      </p>
      <h2>Wyllex is coming soon</h2>
      <p>
        The app is in development and is not yet publicly available. Joining the waitlist is free.
        It does not create a purchase, guarantee an invitation or launch date, or reserve a
        particular price or feature. We will contact you about early access using the email you
        provide.
      </p>
      <h2>What the preview shows</h2>
      <p>
        The website demonstrates our intended product experience. Screens, lesson formats,
        recommendations, focus tools, learning statistics, and progress figures are illustrative
        examples. They are not actual user results or promises about your learning outcomes.
        Features, subject coverage, compatibility, and availability may change before launch.
      </p>
      <h2>Learning, not legal advice</h2>
      <p>
        Educational examples are simplified, introductory material, primarily drawing on UK and EU
        Law. They are not legal advice, a substitute for your university materials, or an
        authoritative statement of current law. Check primary sources, your course requirements, and
        the relevant jurisdiction when studying or applying any rule.
      </p>
      <h2>Joining and leaving</h2>
      <p>
        Please provide an email you are entitled to use. You may leave the waitlist at any time by
        emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}?subject=Unsubscribe`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>{' '}
        with “Unsubscribe” in the subject line. How we use your details is described in our{' '}
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Using the website</h2>
      <p>
        You may browse and share links for personal, lawful purposes. Do not misuse the signup form,
        submit another person’s details without permission, attempt unauthorised access, interfere
        with the site, or use automated tools to collect personal information.
      </p>
      <h2>Our content</h2>
      <p>
        The Wyllex name, original design, illustrations, interface demonstrations, and website copy
        belong to Wyllex or their respective owners. These terms do not grant rights to reproduce or
        commercially exploit them. Other product names mentioned belong to their owners and do not
        imply endorsement or affiliation.
      </p>
      <h2>Availability and responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable care with the website, but do not promise uninterrupted availability or
        that every educational example is complete or current. To the extent permitted by law, we
        are not responsible for loss resulting from reliance on illustrative educational content or
        interruptions beyond our reasonable control. Nothing here excludes liability that cannot
        lawfully be excluded, including liability for fraud, or limits your statutory rights.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes and future app terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the product develops. Any app launch, subscription, or purchase
        will have its own terms presented before you use or buy it. The version on this page applies
        to your current use of this website.
      </p>
      <h2>Governing law and contact</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of {site.legal.jurisdiction}, without removing any
        mandatory protections available where you live. For questions, contact{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
